  CardSpriteHand: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7648f67f8778ab14c95a1597b2307d70, type: 3}
  Placement: 2
  CardStory: 'And I am torn apart.

    

    I feel the briars grow within my
    belly and upwards, crushing my lungs, infesting alveoli with a myriad thorns,
    crushing my ribs and feeding greedily on my marrow. My body contorts, twists
    in ways it was never meant to, but they keep it alive, keep me conscious through
    all of it.

    

    The laughter has stopped. One of them is weeping. Gods,
    I am **hungry.**

    

    My teeth sink deeply into his flesh, ripping him
    apart. I barely hear the screams. I revel in the deep metallic taste, but I enjoy
    most that they suffer instead of me. This is what She promised, a release from
    fear and anguish in exchange for pain. My pain, theirs.

    

    What does
    it matter? I will become a funeral wreath in Her honor, if it gets me my revenge. '
